## API Design

### REST Conventions

| Action | Method | Path | Response |
|--------|--------|------|----------|
| List | GET | `/api/v1/users` | 200 + array |
| Get | GET | `/api/v1/users/:id` | 200 + object |
| Create | POST | `/api/v1/users` | 201 + object |
| Update | PUT | `/api/v1/users/:id` | 200 + object |
| Delete | DELETE | `/api/v1/users/:id` | 204 |

### Validation

- Validate all input at API boundary
- Use [Zod/Joi/class-validator] for schema validation
- Return 400 with validation errors

---

## Security Requirements

### Authentication

- Use [JWT/Session] for authentication
- Tokens expire after [1 hour]
- Refresh tokens valid for [7 days]

### Authorization

- Check permissions before data access
- Use middleware for route protection
- Never expose sensitive data in responses

### Data Protection

- Hash passwords with bcrypt (cost factor 12+)
- Encrypt sensitive data at rest
- Use parameterized queries only (no string concatenation)
- Sanitize all user input

---

## Database

### Query Standards

```typescript
// Always use parameterized queries
const user = await db.query(
  'SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = $1',
  [userId]
);

// Never do this
const user = await db.query(`SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = ${userId}`);
```

### Migrations

- All schema changes require migrations
- Migrations must be reversible
- Test rollback before deploying

